# id: BM81-l1-search-takes-the-wrong-half
# blinds: the binary search over the L1 run landing on the right file
# covering-lane: cpp-test
# expect: killed
# control-lane: cpp-build
# expect-control: alive
#
# THE PROGRESS ASSERTION STAYS TRUE. `hi - lo` shrinks on both branches, so the
# search still terminates -- cleanly, quickly, and on the wrong file. That is
# GF-12 in one line, and it is why this class carries `covers-correctness:`
# rather than `covered-by:`: what catches it is a READ, not a loop invariant.
#
# BM68 is the same shape one level down, in ConcatIter's seek. Two loops, same
# separation, and the separation is the whole of CF-3's point.
